  "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\n{u}^{2}-2au+{a}^{2}=(u-a)^{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-3u+\\frac{9}{4} & = \\\\ {u}^{2}-3u+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ {u}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}u+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ {(u-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({u}^{2}-3u+\\frac{9}{4})+5 & = \\\\ {(u-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+5 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
